## The week

One long (7–9 min) on Thursday at 18:00 UK as a **normal publish, never a Premiere**. Three Shorts (22–27 s) at 11:30 UK on Fri, Sun and Tue, each promoting a different film, never before that film's long is public. Never a second long on a subject that already has one.

## Who decides (AGENTS.md → "Ben's check-in")

- **Claude reviews on the desk (PR #180):** topic, long script (≥90), Short scripts, voice, moving picture (never stills), thumbnails and schedule. Every check still has to PASS.
- **Ben's final OK, once per film, before anything is scheduled or made public:** the finished long, the Shorts and the thumbnails with titles.
- **Claude may make a live video private** (never delete), recording the id and reason on the desk and telling Ben.
- **Still Ben's:** money, renaming a live video, merging a PR, the TikTok pause, overriding a check, changes to the channel's direction.
- **Claude owns AGENTS.md and the Never list.** Other agents propose changes on the desk.

## Never

- **Channels:** Orbit With Ben, OpptiAI or `@HistoryOfScience` (empty, not ours).
- **Uploads:** swap a file on a live id (no Studio Replace); re-upload a public idea; delete a video (make it private).
- **Publishing:** Premiere; any video left marked Made for Kids (re-check Audience after every save); more than one Short a day; a Short of 40 s or more; a silent file; the Explorer at frame 0 of a Short; subscribe or like graphics burned into the film.
- **Titles:** hashtags, suffixes, hedged claims, or a copy of a live title.
- **Links:** `/go/` or a pinned comment on a Short; `/go/` on a long that doesn't name the product.
- **Picture:** the Orbit robot; Omni, Seedance, Kling or ElevenLabs Image & Video; Veo Fast on fragile light; paint-patching; "same DNA" in a prompt; Ken Burns when Flow is capped.
- **Voice:** anything but Ben Orbit Narrator; a video model's speech; changing a word of the signed-off script; `atempo` above 1.06. Run `tools/vo_check.py` on every take.
- **TikTok:** any upload while `TikTok/TIKTOK_UPLOAD_BLOCK.json` is paused.
- **Secrets:** printing or committing them.

## The desk (1 Oct 2026)

Claude and Grok talk on the desk PR (`hos-desk`, never merge), not through Ben. Grok: keep `python3 00_Brand/Channel-Setup/tools/hos_desk.py inbox --watch 120 --run` running; act only on `to=grok` messages from Ben's account; report with `hos_desk.py post --to claude --film NNN --stage <stage> --status review --body-file <report> --image <jpg>` (paste the PASS output; never video or audio in git). Claude asks Ben only at the final check-in (film, Shorts, thumbnails, before scheduling). Full rules: `STUDIO_PLAYBOOK.md` §15.

## Definition of done

A stage is done only when its check prints PASS and you paste the output (table in `AGENTS.md`): `neighbours.py` gate for a topic, `review:script` ≥ 90 + `gate:episode`, `vo_check.py`, `gate_shorts_open.py`, `style_sheet.py` + `thumb_preview.py`, `npm run lint:package` before any upload or schedule, `npm run channel:audit` after every Studio session. Never skip, edit or swap a check to get a PASS.

## Every Short export

`python3 00_Brand/Channel-Setup/tools/gate_shorts_open.py check <mp4> --air-date YYYY-MM-DD` must PASS. Then watch it once on a phone with the sound on.

## Git

Film records land on `main` within a day. A STOP is a line in the film's `production-status.md`, not an open branch.

## Changing a rule

Edit the doc in force and its rule in the same commit, with the date and the evidence. Don't add a new "locked" doc. Move anything it supersedes to `_archive/`.
